1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:01,918
[CALOY] <i>I'm ready.</i>

2
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,002
<i>I'm on my way to Billy's.</i>

3
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:04,337
[RAIN] <i>Is this true?</i>

4
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:06,172
<i>Caloy escaped!</i>

5
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:08,133
[SPRAY PAINT HISSING]

6
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:09,968
- [BILLY GRUNTS]
- [BODY THUDS]

7
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,762
<i>- Stop it!</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

8
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:14,514
<i>Shut up--</i> [CALOY YELPS]

9
00:00:14,597 --> 00:00:16,474
- [BILLY YELPS, GROANS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

10
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,104
<i>My God, Billy!</i>

11
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:22,731
<i>Billy!</i>

12
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:23,648
<i>Billy?</i>

13
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:26,025
<i>Help! Please help us!</i>

14
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:27,360
<i>Billy? Billy!</i>

15
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,946
<i>My God, Billy, what happened?</i>

16
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>Billy! Billy. Billy.</i>

17
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,409
<i>Help!</i>

18
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,119
<i>Please help us!</i>

19
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,621
<i>Billy? Billy, Billy, Billy.</i>

20
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,914
<i>My God!</i>

21
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:41,124
<i>Jordan!</i>

22
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,835
<i>Jordan, help me!</i>

23
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:46,045
<i>- Auntie Pres!</i>
<i>- Billy?</i>

24
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:48,006
<i>- What happened to Billy?</i>
<i>- Watch her for a second.</i>

25
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,883
<i>I'll call an ambulance.</i>

26
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,800
<i>Dude!</i>

27
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:54,387
[CALOY] <i>She fought back, so I beat her up.</i>
<i>I slammed her head against the wall.</i>

28
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:55,680
[BEA] <i>For heaven's sake, Caloy!</i>

29
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:56,890
<i>Why did you hurt her?</i>

30
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:59,976
<i>You were just supposed to spray-paint</i>
<i>their walls to scare her! That's it!</i>

31
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,228
<i>Why did you hurt her?</i>

32
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,314
<i>He hurt Billy?</i>

33
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:06,357
<i>Serves her right!</i>

34
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:08,610
<i>Come on, 'Bi…</i>

35
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:12,489
<i>You were detained.</i>

36
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,699
<i>You lost your job.</i>

37
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,326
<i>You've got a case against you.</i>

38
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:19,537
<i>And all of that happened because of Billy.</i>

39
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,460
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- Dude.</i>

40
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,544
<i>How do you feel?</i>

41
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,296
<i>What about Oliver?</i>

42
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:31,716
<i>And Auntie Pres? Where are they?</i>

43
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>They're safe.</i>

44
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:34,886
<i>Dude, you scared the shit out of me.</i>

45
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:37,931
<i>Sorry.</i>

46
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,391
<i>When are they going to stop?</i>

47
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:44,687
<i>What they're doing to us</i>
<i>just keeps getting worse.</i>

48
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,065
<i>What matters is you're okay.</i>

49
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:48,775
<i>What if…?</i>

50
00:01:48,858 --> 00:01:53,363
<i>I just don't know what I would do if…</i>

51
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,449
<i>I'm just glad you're okay.</i>

52
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,371
[ENRICO] <i>What happened here?</i>

53
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:05,291
<i>Someone broke in. The intruder</i>
<i>even spray-painted their walls.</i>

54
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:08,044
<i>How are the people who live here?</i>
<i>Where are they?</i>

55
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:10,630
[NEIGHBOR]
<i>Billy probably got hurt fighting back.</i>

56
00:02:10,713 --> 00:02:12,632
<i>They took her to the hospital.</i>

57
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,302
<i>Nurse, which room is Benilda Cariño in?</i>

58
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,346
<i>Okay, sir. Hold on.</i>

59
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:20,765
<i>I'll check which room she's in.</i>

60
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:23,393
<i>Cariño…</i>

61
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:34,028
- A cup of coffee, please.
- Okay.

62
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:37,198
Jordan, Billy is asleep.

63
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:39,784
The doctor gave her a painkiller.

64
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:44,038
Are you sure I don't need
to go back there, Auntie?

65
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:47,375
Yeah. I'll look after her for now.

66
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,919
[PHONE CHIMES]

67
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:57,635
I'VE BEEN TEXTING YOU FOR HOURS.

68
00:02:57,719 --> 00:03:02,307
WHEN ARE WE MEETING UP AGAIN?

69
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:09,063
Are you free tomorrow?

70
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:10,940
SORRY, BRANDON. MAYBE NEXT TIME.

71
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,984
WE HAVE A FAMILY EMERGENCY.

72
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:21,701
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:08,122
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:28,559
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:47,912
Dad?

76
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:54,043
Billy? Sweetie?

77
00:04:54,127 --> 00:05:00,925
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO"
BY SHANIAH ROLLO PLAYING]

78
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,477
<i>Dad…</i>

79
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:15,690
<i>Are you leaving?</i>

80
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,445
<i>What time are you coming home?</i>

81
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,867
<i>I'll wait for you, Dad.</i>

82
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:30,413
<i>I'll miss you.</i>

83
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:36,002
[SOBS]

84
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:42,967
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

85
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:06,365
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

86
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:26,177
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

87
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:45,488
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

88
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:07,260
["MAG-ISA NA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

89
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:26,237
[BIRDS TWITTERING]

90
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,407
They're installing the last one.
They're almost done.

91
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:30,741
They also arrived on time.

92
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,702
Thanks for the recommendation.

93
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:35,955
<i>Hopefully, with all the CCTV cameras</i>
<i>you had installed,</i>

94
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:38,458
<i>Caloy and Bea won't even</i>
<i>think of going back there.</i>

95
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,168
Rightly so.

96
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,421
Charm, thank you.
I'll make it up to you tomorrow.

97
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:45,840
Okay, bye.

98
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:48,801
- Ma'am, it's done. Everything's installed.
- All done?

99
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,428
[BILLY] Okay, let me check it.

100
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,974
Okay. It's working now, sir.

101
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:56,309
- Thank you.
- [MAN] Okay.

102
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,935
- Here's your payment.
- Thank you.

103
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:04,108
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:23,544
[PHONE RINGING]

105
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:27,423
Hello?

106
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:30,134
Hello? What's taking you
so long to respond?

107
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:32,929
So, can I see you tomorrow?

108
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,222
Brandon…

109
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:36,265
Brandon, I'm sorry.

110
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:38,142
I'm not available.

111
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,852
You always say that.

112
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,896
You're just making up
excuses at this point.

113
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:44,190
What? Have you changed your mind about me?

114
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:46,526
Don't be dramatic. It's not like that.

115
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:51,697
There's a lot going on at home,
so I don't have time to see you.

116
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:56,369
Brandon, we're going to eat,
so I'm hanging up. Bye.

117
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,205
He… Hello?

118
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:00,414
Hello?

119
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,670
[PHONE CHIMES]

120
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:10,091
YOU'RE ALWAYS CANCELING

121
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:15,846
- [BILLY] Auntie Pres?
- Yes?

122
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,848
- The CCTV cameras are done.
- Oh, okay.

123
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,725
Billy, I have something to give to you.

124
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,185
- One for you, one for me.
- Mm-hmm.

125
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:22,603
There you go.

126
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,897
This is how you use it.

127
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,566
- Remove this side.
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.

128
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:27,984
- Aim at their eyes.
- Yes.

129
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:29,777
- Press it. Aim towards the bad guy.
- Copy.

130
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,946
I know how to use it, Auntie. Thank you.

131
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:34,782
- Okay. Here.
- Sorry for making you worried.

132
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:37,118
Hey, don't worry about it.
You're not a burden.

133
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:39,328
What bothers me is the people
who are pestering you.

134
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:41,789
They're the ones
who should apologize to me.

135
00:09:41,872 --> 00:09:43,416
Always have that in your bag.

136
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:46,043
- Bring it with you. Okay?
- Yes, I promise.

137
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,753
All right, come on. Let's eat.

138
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,046
- Let's go.
- Okay.

139
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,134
[PRECIOUS] Fortunately,
I managed to get some stock.

140
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,596
Come on, let's eat.

141
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,097
Okay.

142
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,141
Do you want some fish?

143
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:02,143
- Okay, Auntie.
- I'll put it on your plate.

144
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,896
Hey.

145
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,940
Is your head aching again?

146
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:10,276
No, Auntie Pres.

147
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,863
I just remembered something
that was like a dream.

148
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,451
What was it?

149
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:22,622
[OLIVER] Auntie, Billy, look.

150
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,206
I learned something new.

151
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,541
- [WHOOSHES]
- [EXHALES SHARPLY]

152
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,127
- This is called "jab, slip."
- [BILLY] Wow.

153
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:30,212
[OLIVER] I'm going to use it
when the thief comes back.

154
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:31,589
I'll knock him out.

155
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,841
Oh, no. No. Come, sit here.

156
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,509
I have something to tell you.

157
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:39,472
Starting tomorrow,
I'll be going to school with you.

158
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:40,681
I'll stay there and watch you.

159
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,558
I already filed for leave.

160
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,476
What?

161
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:45,144
Why?

162
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:49,231
Sir Eric is there
to defend me from bullies.

163
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,983
Besides, I can take on Biboy myself.

164
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:53,027
No, no. You can't change my mind.

165
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,529
I'll stay there and watch you, okay?

166
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:58,366
I can manage on my own, Auntie.

167
00:10:58,449 --> 00:10:59,450
[PRECIOUS] Mm…

168
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:02,495
He's a big boy now.

169
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:05,581
I don't think he wants me
to accompany him, Billy.

170
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:08,584
Didn't he use to cry so much

171
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,336
whenever we took him to school?

172
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:13,964
Didn't he used to cling to my legs?
[FAKE SOBS]

173
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:16,467
[OLIVER] Well, it's different now.

174
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,052
- Hmm?
- [PRECIOUS] Hmph!

175
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:21,514
- You're still that baby, right?
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]

176
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:23,474
- You're our baby.
- Baby.

177
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:26,268
- No! No!
- You're still a baby.

178
00:11:26,352 --> 00:11:27,603
- Baby.
- Smells like a baby.

179
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,647
- No, no, no!
- You're our baby.

180
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:30,773
- Right?
- No!

181
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,942
- You're still a baby.
- I'm not a baby!

182
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:34,652
- Drink your water, baby.
- No!

183
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,532
The blotter and medico-legal report

184
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:41,826
of Carlos Toledo's assault
have been filed.

185
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:45,621
His records also include
vandalism on your property.

186
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:47,748
We will keep monitoring it.

187
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,584
Sir, what's the update on Bea Mercado?

188
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:53,671
Bea Mercado has been under surveillance
since last week.

189
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:57,508
I had some officers
go to their house for questioning.

190
00:11:58,134 --> 00:12:00,719
You can count on us. Don't worry.

191
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:03,305
We will do our best.

192
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:07,726
You know, that's what you guys always say.

193
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,521
But nothing ever happens.

194
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:13,983
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [MOUTHS SOFTLY] Calm down.

195
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:27,079
[PHONE RINGS]

196
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,082
Hello, Brandon.

197
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:33,461
I already told you yesterday.
I can't meet up with you.

198
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:36,672
It's not that I want
to end things between us,

199
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:39,925
but I really need to go with Oliver.

200
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,136
I'll be there in a bit.

201
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,555
You can leave Oliver alone for a moment.

202
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:47,600
Huh? Oh, I really can't.

203
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,810
I'm on my way.

204
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:53,939
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:58,027
Uh, Precious, excuse me,
and please don't be offended.

206
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:00,029
But it's okay, you can leave.

207
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:02,698
Since I'm here, I can look after Oliver.

208
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:06,952
Oh, you don't have to. It's okay.
Thank you, Sir Eric.

209
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,288
I'm surprised admin allowed you.

210
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:12,458
I heard parents and guardians
aren't allowed to wait here.

211
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:16,837
They allow exemptions,
especially in special cases.

212
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:19,256
Special case? Why?
What happened to Oliver?

213
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,841
Uh…

214
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:25,179
Nothing happened to Oliver.

215
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:27,723
Someone broke into our front yard
the other night.

216
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,683
We already reported it to the police.

217
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:33,479
But I'm worried whoever broke in
might come back,

218
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:35,189
so I'm watching him in school.

219
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:37,775
Come back? What? Why?

220
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:40,319
Oh, no reason.
I'm just not taking any chances.

221
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:42,696
Well, yes. As a parent,

222
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:46,242
you really feel more at ease
when your child is with you.

223
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:50,746
Have some refreshments.

224
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,045
Ma'am, sir.

225
00:13:58,629 --> 00:13:59,964
I'll do it.

226
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:01,632
I'll tell the truth.

227
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:05,469
That Caloy guy…

228
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:08,389
He courted me before.

229
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:12,184
But I turned him down.

230
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:15,729
I mean, it's like he's obsessed with me.

231
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:19,650
I kept rejecting him,
but he remained persistent.

232
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:22,987
This is different
from your previous statement.

233
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:24,738
Why are you only saying this now?

234
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,869
Because

235
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,954
I'm scared of Caloy.

236
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,831
He's obsessed with me.

237
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:38,794
I thought he might hurt me
if I reported him and ratted him out.

238
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:42,172
Are you saying that
you have nothing to do with this?

239
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:43,799
Here.

240
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:48,387
What's this? Where is this?

241
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:50,222
I have no idea.
I had nothing to do with it.

242
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,767
Billy Cariño's house.

243
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,605
Billy's house?

244
00:14:59,857 --> 00:15:01,942
He has actually lost it. Look, Ma.

245
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,570
- He's crazy.
- Oh, right.

246
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:06,822
He is. He's crazy.

247
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:09,783
Did he do anything to Billy?

248
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:13,662
He assaulted Ms. Cariño.

249
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:15,539
He hurt Billy?!

250
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,207
[BEA] That's insane.

251
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:20,377
See? I told you. He's obsessed with me.

252
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:22,671
How's Billy? Is she okay?

253
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:27,301
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:30,012
You know, sir, ma'am…

255
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:35,184
I feel like Caloy found out.

256
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:38,520
Caloy found out that I didn't like Billy.

257
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:39,980
So he did that.

258
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:43,233
He probably thought
I'd be happy with what he did.

259
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:47,404
I told you that he was obsessed with me.

260
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:49,490
He's charmed by my beauty.

261
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:51,283
So it's really scary.

262
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:55,955
Whenever he'd come here,
we never let him in.

263
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:59,541
Because I'm terrified
of what he might do to my Bea.

264
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:02,336
So, please help us.

265
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:05,339
Catch him and put him behind bars.

266
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:07,424
That's right, ma'am.

267
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:11,387
Also, we need protection.

268
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:15,432
Maybe you can give us a bodyguard too.

269
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,101
For our own safety.

270
00:16:17,184 --> 00:16:18,560
A bodyguard?

271
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:23,440
The report claims
you might have instructed Toledo

272
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,818
to cause trouble at Billy Cariño's house.

273
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,236
[MARIELA] No…

274
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:28,862
Me?

275
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:31,156
I would never do that, ma'am!

276
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,700
Why would I?

277
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:34,326
Who even told you that?

278
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,786
You know what? Just prove it!

279
00:16:35,869 --> 00:16:38,914
And if you do,
I'll take myself to the police station

280
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:41,333
and have myself locked up!

281
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:42,751
Believe me, I'll do that!

282
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:45,087
[BEA HUFFING]

283
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,424
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

284
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:51,176
Look, I still have to get ready for work.

285
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,845
Do you have any more questions?

286
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:54,471
No, that's all.

287
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,682
We'll just get back to you.

288
00:16:56,765 --> 00:16:57,725
Goodbye.

289
00:16:57,808 --> 00:16:59,101
[MARIELA] Thank you.

290
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:05,858
That Billy can go to hell.

291
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:09,737
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:10,946
Uh…

293
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,156
Ma. [CHUCKLES DRYLY]

294
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:14,825
Don't give it too much thought. [HUFFS]
It's nothing.

295
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:16,035
[SCOFFS]

296
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:18,954
I'll take care of it. Don't worry, okay?

297
00:17:19,663 --> 00:17:21,373
Calm down, calm down.

298
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,916
[MUSIC SWELLING]

299
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,209
[MUSIC FADES]

300
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:35,262
[LOW ELECTRICAL HUM]

301
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:37,431
[MARIELA GROANS]
Damn it!

302
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:40,434
The power's gone!

303
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:44,229
Uh, Ma, don't worry. Okay?

304
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:45,814
I've already applied for work.

305
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,650
Once I'm hired,
I'll request an advance on my salary

306
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:51,653
so we can cover the rent and power bill.

307
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,740
Don't worry, Ma.
Everything is going to be fine.

308
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,408
No.

309
00:17:56,492 --> 00:18:00,496
We won't have any peace
until that Billy leaves us alone!

310
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,956
I'm sure she's behind the cops showing up!

311
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:04,750
Sure, but let it go.

312
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:06,460
She'll stop eventually.

313
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,337
When?

314
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,505
When you're locked up?

315
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:10,923
- Look, if you want--
- [KNIFE THUDS]

316
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:11,965
[BEA] Uh, Ma…

317
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,884
What I want

318
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,720
is for you to let me deal with Billy.

319
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:19,389
I'll handle her, okay?

320
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,642
Ma, listen. I can do that.

321
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,393
Ma, look at me.

322
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,729
Look at me, Ma. Swear to me.

323
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:29,066
Ma, promise me this. Okay?

324
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:32,194
Billy is mine. Leave her to me, okay?

325
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:33,487
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:34,947
Okay?

327
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,115
Ma?

328
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:38,951
- That's a promise, okay?
- Mmm.

329
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:42,955
Okay, I'll leave now.

330
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:45,916
Bye, Ma.

331
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,920
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

332
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:57,010
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:01,974
[DRAMATIC STING]

334
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:15,946
<i>They have to pay for what they did.</i>
<i>Before they do anything else.</i>

335
00:19:16,029 --> 00:19:18,115
<i>I just realized</i>
<i>how important she is to me.</i>

336
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:21,869
<i>Wish me luck actually</i>
<i>falling asleep tonight.</i>

337
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,787
<i>- Do you want me to go there?</i>
<i>- Huh?</i>

338
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,080
<i>I'm back to square one.</i>

339
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:28,417
<i>That should've been mine,</i>
<i>but Billy just had to steal it!</i>

340
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,918
<i>Just use me.</i>

341
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,879
<i>I'll get back at Billy.</i>

342
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:34,756
[MARIELA] <i>That Billy can't</i>
<i>look down on you now!</i>

343
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:38,427
<i>Is there really no way we can look</i>
<i>at Mariela Mercado's files?</i>

344
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,470
<i>Bea has a huge grudge against you.</i>

345
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:44,808
<i>I hope we finally learn why.</i>
<i>My family's safety is at stake here.</i>

346
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:48,020
<i>I don't know why she hates Billy so much,</i>

347
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:51,315
<i>to the point that she even</i>
<i>conspired with a criminal.</i>

348
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,482
<i>A criminal?</i>

349
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:56,278
[BILLY] <i>A woman has been standing</i>
<i>outside for a while now.</i>

350
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:57,487
<i>I can't make her out clearly.</i>

351
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:59,114
<i>- I'll check it out.</i>
<i>- No, you won't!</i>

352
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,032
<i>Ma?</i>

353
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,326
<i>Ma?</i>

354
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:08,373
[MARIELA] <i>I can't bear to</i>
<i>see you suffer, my dear.</i>
